BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261002T140945Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260918
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260919
UID:calendar-event-8559021916@schoology.com
URL;VALUE=URI:http://schoology.tesd.net/assignment/8544428142
SUMMARY:Global Perspectives Formative Assessment (Written)
DESCRIPTION:This is an open note in-class assessment and will be a mix between  \nmultiple-choice and free response. Listed below are the directions for the  \nfree response section.\n\n \n\nDirections: The following essential question will be answered to conclude our  \nGlobal Perspectives unit. You will handwrite your answer the following  \nquestion in complete sentences using specific details from class materials in  \na 1-paragraph response. You should answer the question\, provide specific  \nexamples\, and explain how the examples answer the question. Your paragraph  \nshould be 6-9 sentences long.\n\n \n\nThis will be completed in class on Friday 9/18 as part of your Unit 0  \nFormative Assessment.\n\n \n\n \n\nEssential Question: Why is perspective important in the study of world  \nhistory?\n\n \n\nInclude examples from the options below:\n\n * What is History lesson (Brief History of Lawns)\n * Chapters 1 and 2 of your textbook\n * World as 100 People\n * Guns\, Germs\, and Steel\n * Definitions\n * Nacirema Reading\n * We and They Poem\n\n \n\n \n\nCriteria\n\n5\n\n4\n\n3\n\n2\n\n1\n\nAnswer\n\nEssential question is thoroughly answered\n\nResponse is mostly focused on answering the essential question\n\nResponse doesn't answer the full question or loses focus\n\nResponse doesn't answer the full question AND loses focus\n\nResponse doesn't address the question at all\n\nEvidence\n\nMore than two specific examples are included\n\nTwo specific examples are included\n\nOnly one example included\n\nExamples included without detail\n\nNo examples provided\n\nExplanation\n\nAll evidence is used to support answer using in-depth analysis\n\nMost evidence is used to support answer using in-depth analysis\n\nSome evidence is used to support answer\n\nBarely any evidence is used to answer the question\n\nConnections are not explicitly made\n\nMechanics\n\nWriting has little to no errors\n\nA few small errors\n\nMore than a few errors\n\nMany errors throughout\n\nReadability is limited by errors in mechanics\n\n \n\n*Up to five points may be deducted if the paragraph doesn't meet the length  \nrequirement\n\n  - Link: http://schoology.tesd.net/assignment/8544428142
END:VEVENT
