SUMMARY:Coming of Age 4-Paragraph Assignment
DESCRIPTION:*Coming of Age 4-Paragraph Writing Assignment*\n\n*Through the Clever dashboard\, open Turnitin.com. All work needs to be  \ncompleted within this platform. *\n\nOver the last couple weeks\, we’ve focused our conversations and work on  \ncoming-of-age stories. We have focused on how charactes change to come of  \nage. We have looked at how these aspects come up for Jay in /Patron Saints of  \nNothing\,/ Waverly in “Rules of the Game\,” and Anisa in "The Truth About  \nOwls\," and even Gilgamesh from /The Epic of Gilgamesh/. \n\nPrompt: Consider the experiences of Jay and one other protagonist (choose  \neither Waverly or Anisa or Gilgamesh). Discuss how the characters *change to  \ncoming of age*. \n\nIntroduction: should now include two titles and authors and a progression  \nfrom a general idea about coming of age to a thesis as the last sentence  \n(which should include two characters).  \n\nOne paragraph should be devoted to Jay’s coming of age and maturation  \nthrough his growth.\n\nThe other paragraph should be devoted to the second character's coming of age  \nand maturation through hers or his growth.\n\nQuote and cite the texts twice in each body paragraph. Use one of the four  \nmethods of integration each time you quote and cite the text.\n\n            For example… method #1 – Context and signal phrase\n\nAs Jay begins to tell his father about his trip to the Philippines\, Jay  \nthinks\, “But there are good things I can hold on to\, and there are other  \nthings I have the power to change” (Ribay 318).\n\nConclusion Paragraph: Reword your thesis and then... reach a conclusion by  \nconsidering the big picture. Address theme rather than repeating information  \nfrom the previous paragraphs.\n\n \n\nIntroduction starts general\, includes background info.\, ends with thesis\n\n5 Points\n\nBody paragraphs begin with topic sentences\, include accurate examples as  \nevidence\, and provide reasoning/commentary on evidence. References to texts  \nare clear and purposeful. Textual evidence is properly punctuated\,  \nintegrated\, and effective in supporting the essay’s topic. \n\n15 Points\n\nConclusion addresses the big picture (theme) rather than repeating info. \n\n5 Points\n\nEvidence of proofreading\, editing including third person point of view\,  \npresent tense verbs to write about literature\, MLA formatting (heading\,  \nspacing\, font\, citations). \n\n15 Points\n\n* *\n\n* * - Link: http://schoology.tesd.net/assignment/8528304855
